VGG16 Transfer Learning for Flower Classification
Objective
Implement transfer learning using the pre-trained VGG16 model for classifying flower images and evaluate its performance.

Dataset
This project uses the TensorFlow Flower Photos Dataset.
Dataset URL:
https://storage.googleapis.com/download.tensorflow.org/example_images/flower_photos.tgz
The dataset contains 3,670 images belonging to 5 flower classes:
Daisy
Dandelion
Roses
Sunflowers
Tulips
Dataset Split:
80% Training: 2,936 images
20% Validation: 734 images
Image Size: 224 × 224
Batch Size: 32

Model
A VGG16 model pre-trained on ImageNet is used as the feature extractor.
Pre-trained convolutional layers are frozen.
Original ImageNet classification layer is removed.
New classification layers are added for the 5 flower classes.
Final layer uses Softmax activation.

Architecture
Input Image (224×224×3)
        ↓
Pre-trained VGG16
        ↓
Global Average Pooling
        ↓
Dense (128)
        ↓
Dropout (0.5)
        ↓
Dense (5, Softmax)

Training
Optimizer : Adam
Loss      : Sparse Categorical Crossentropy
Epochs    : 5
Metric    : Accuracy

Execution
1. Download the Flower Photos dataset.
2. Load and split the dataset into training and validation sets.
3. Load pre-trained VGG16.
4. Freeze the base model and add a classification layer.
5. Train for 5 epochs.
6. Evaluate validation accuracy and loss.
7. Plot training and validation accuracy.

